X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Adventures": "https://www.meetup.com/adventures/events/317431796/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_adventures
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Triangle Hiking & Outdoors
UID:event_317431796@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261121T065017Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T053000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T220000
SUMMARY:(Day Trip) Volunteer Project/Waterfalls/Fire Tower: Blue Ridge Par
 kway
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nJoin me in this one-day ad
 venture and volunteer effort which starts with helping Waterfall Keepers o
 f North Carolina with its Adopt-A-Highway cleanup effort near Asheville. I
 t's an early start but it'll be worth it.\n\nThe rewards for this 1-2hr ef
 fort? Helping keep the areas near waterfalls clean PLUS the chance to expl
 ore some great waterfalls near and along the Blue Ridge Parkway close to G
 raveyard Fields\, including Second Falls\, Sunburst Falls and Skinny Dip F
 alls. In addition\, we'll take a walk up Frying Pan Mountain Fire Tower to
  see incredible views from the top. These are all can't miss places and wa
 terfalls to visit.\n\nWe'll meet in Chapel Hill at 5:30AM. We'll then driv
 e to near Sunburst Falls south of Canton to meet with the Waterfall Keeper
 s of NC group around 10AM. Once we're done with our 1-mile stretch\, we'll
  breakaway to have lunch at Current Tavern in Canton then explore the diff
 erent waterfalls\, BRP and Frying Pan Mountain Fire Tower.\n\nBring: Cloth
 ing layers\, daypack for the short hikes\, Garden or utility type gloves i
 f you have a pair (if not\, WKNC can provide gloves to you. Good footwear.
  We'll stop for food during this trip.\nIMPORTANT: RSVP's close at 3PM on 
 Friday so I can let Kevin Adams know how many people will be on my team he
 lping.\n\nBy participating in this event\, you agree to the terms below:\n
 TRIP PARTICIPANT WAIVER OF LIABILITY I fully realize that this activity in
 volves a risk of personal injury\, property damage\, or loss of my person 
 or property. I hereby for myself\, my heirs\, executors and administrators
 \, and same for persons with whom are in my party\, waive and release any 
 claims or rights against Triangle Hiking & Outdoors Group (THOG)\, all of 
 its owners and coordinators for any and all injury\, damages or loss to my
  person or property incurred during this activity. I also understand that 
 THOG organizers are not required\, nor should it be assumed that they are 
 CPR/First Aid/Wilderness Survival Certified and I am responsible for my ow
 n personal safety.\nQuestions or comments about this event?\nPlease commen
 t below or message me on Meetup.\n-Larredo
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/adventures/events/317431796/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261114T192228Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261114T192228Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
