DESCRIPTION:Friends of Lower Haw is offering a program on ecotones\, transi
 tional areas of vegetation where different natural communities meet. Examp
 les of ecotones include transitional areas between forest and meadow\, or 
 between riverbank and water body. Our guide will be naturalist and nature 
 photographer Jason Brown. We’ll visit transition areas where birds and w
 ildlife can be spotted. Our guide will also talk about how past land use a
 nd land management has had an influence on the flora and fauna occurring a
 t the Lower Haw River State Natural Area. This event is free and open to t
 he public.  All ages are welcome.
GEO:35.771669;-79.142253
LOCATION:Bynum Mill Access at Lower Haw River State Natural Area
SUMMARY:Ecotones: Transitional Zones Where Ecosystems Meet
