DESCRIPTION:Free Online Discussion for North Carolina Teachers\nThursday\, 
 December 3rd | 7pm – 7:45 pm via Zoom \nRegister Here \n\nJoin Christie 
 Norris\, DNCR Director of Education\, and the North Carolina Council for t
 he Social Studies to learn about the incredible K-12 opportunities availab
 le through the North Carolina Department of Natural and Cultural Resources
  (DNCR). With more than 100 museums\, historic sites\, state parks\, aquar
 iums\, libraries\, archives\, and educational programs across North Caroli
 na\, DNCR helps bring learning to life through hands-on experiences\, fiel
 d trips\, classroom resources\, educator professional development\, teache
 r travel programs\, North Carolina History Day\, and more.\n\nFive teacher
 s who join us for the session will be randomly selected to receive a copy 
 of DNCR’s youth publication & tote bag\, Within Our Power: The Story of 
 the Edenton Ladies' Tea Party.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Learning Across NC with DNCR
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/learning-across-nc-with-dncr
