X-SOURCE-URLS:{"NC Museum of Natural Sciences": "https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/project-restore-educator-trek-waterdog-warriors/", "NC Cultural Resources": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/project-restore-educator-trek-waterdog-warriors"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Naturalsciences": "https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/project-restore-educator-trek-waterdog-warriors/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:naturalsciences
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources, NC Museum of Natural Sciences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261205T170000
DTSTAMP:20261121T015035
CREATED:20220927T204406Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261117T141627Z
UID:78003-1796461200-1796490000@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Project RESTORE Educator Trek: Waterdog Warriors
DESCRIPTION:Date: Saturday\, December 5\, 2026. Please also mark your calendar for a rain date on Sunday\, December 6!\nTimes: 9am to 5pm \nJoin us in the search for one of North Carolina’s rarest salamanders\, the federally threatened Neuse River waterdog\, found only in the Neuse and Tar-Pamlico River Basins in North Carolina. Learn from expert biologists\, explore the natural history of the waterdog\, observe historically collected specimens and participate in field monitoring of the species. Discover how you can bring the excitement of field research of this rare species into your classroom. \nWith support from the US Fish and Wildlife Service\, Project RESTORE (Rescuing Endangered Species Through Outreach\, Restoration\, and Education) will feature a suite of educational opportunities for teachers and students to participate in restoration and monitoring of imperiled and endangered species in eastern North Carolina. \nLocations/Transportation: We will meet at the Museum in downtown Raleigh before heading to field sites in Johnston County. You can leave your vehicle parked in Raleigh and ride in Museum vans; we will return to Raleigh by 5pm. \nCredit: 8 contact hours toward CEUs or Criteria II/III for North Carolina’s Environmental Education Certification Program \nRegistration: This workshop is FULL\, please join our waiting list! \nThe full workshop fee is due when you register and payment is via credit card. Registration for most Educator Treks is on a first-come\, first-served basis. Treks fill quickly\, so register early!
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/project-restore-educator-trek-waterdog-warriors/
LOCATION:Nature Exploration Center\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Educator Treks,Educators,Environmental Conference Center,Trips,Workshops
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan%20Davis":MAILTO:megan.davis@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822735;-78.6395502
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Nature Exploration Center 11 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=11 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6395502,35.7822735
END:VEVENT
