X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/new-bern-to-celebrate-bill-of-rights-day-with-historic-new-bern-resolves-marker-dedication"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261121T065024Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54559834169960
DTSTART:20261215T190000Z
DTEND:20261215T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:SAR and DAR Chapters Join Together to Honor America’s Foundin
 g Principles and New Bern’s Revolutionary Heritage During the Nation’s
  250th Anniversary Year\n\nNEW BERN\, NORTH CAROLINA — On Tuesday\, Dece
 mber 15\, 2026\, at 2:00 p.m.\, the New Bern Chapter\, Sons of the America
 n Revolution (SAR) and the Richard Dobbs Spaight Chapter of the National S
 ociety Daughters of the American Revolution (NSDAR) will present a special
  Bill of Rights Day commemoration and the dedication of a new granite and 
 bronze marker honoring the historic New Bern Resolves.\n\nThe ceremony wil
 l take place at Patriot Square at City Hall\, located at 300 Pollock Stree
 t in downtown New Bern.\n\nThe event brings together two important milesto
 nes in American history: the ratification of the United States Bill of Rig
 hts on December 15\, 1791\, and the adoption of the New Bern Resolves in A
 ugust 1774\, during the First Provincial Congress that was held in the the
 n Thirteen Colonies.\n\nThe Bill of Rights: Protecting America’s Fundame
 ntal Freedoms\n\nOn December 15\, 1791\, the first ten amendments to the U
 nited States Constitution were ratified\, becoming known as the Bill of Ri
 ghts.\n\nOriginally proposed by Congress in 1789\, these amendments establ
 ished essential protections against government infringement of individual 
 liberties. Among them are freedom of speech\, religion\, the press\, peace
 ful assembly\, and petition\; protections against unreasonable searches an
 d seizures\; and important guarantees of due process and fair treatment un
 der the law.\n\nThe 2026 commemoration marks the 235th anniversary of this
  historic achievement and provides an opportunity to reflect upon the endu
 ring importance of constitutional rights and responsibilities.\n\nThe New 
 Bern Resolves: A Defining Moment in North Carolina History\n\nNew Bern hol
 ds a significant place in America’s Revolutionary story.\n\nOn August 25
 \, 1774\, seventy-one delegates from across North Carolina assembled in Ne
 w Bern for not only the “first” North Carolina Provincial Congress\, b
 ut the very first Provincial Congress held in all of the Thirteen Colonies
 . Meeting in defiance of British royal authority\, the delegates gathered 
 to address growing grievances concerning taxation\, representation\, and t
 he actions of the British government.\n\nDuring the three-day gathering\, 
 delegates adopted a series of resolutions that became known as the New Ber
 n Resolves.\n\nThese resolutions expressed opposition to British policies 
 and affirmed the colonists’ determination to defend their rights. The Co
 ngress also selected William Hooper\, Joseph Hewes\, and Richard Caswell t
 o represent North Carolina at the First Continental Congress in Philadelph
 ia.\n\nThe New Bern Resolves became an important milestone in North Caroli
 na’s growing resistance to British rule and helped set the stage for the
  American Revolution.\n\nThe commemorative event flyer features an artisti
 c depiction of the signing of the United States Constitution\, recognizing
  a New Bern native\, Richard Dobbs Spaight’s place among the nation’s 
 Founding Fathers.\n\nHis story provides an important historical connection
  between New Bern’s Revolutionary heritage\, the establishment of the Un
 ited States Constitution\, and the fundamental liberties protected by the 
 Bill of Rights.\n\nPreserving History for Future Generations\n\nA highligh
 t of the December 15th ceremony will be the formal dedication of the new N
 ew Bern Resolves Granite & Bronze Marker at Patriot Square.\n\nThe marker 
 will serve as a lasting reminder of New Bern’s contribution to the found
 ing of our nation and provide residents and visitors with an opportunity t
 o learn about this significant chapter of American history.\n\nThe ceremon
 y will also feature a presentation on the history and importance of the Bi
 ll of Rights\, along with live musket volleys by the New Bern Chapter SAR 
 Musket Cadre.\n\nHonoring America’s 250th Anniversary\n\nAs the United S
 tates commemorates the 250th anniversary of the Declaration of Independenc
 e in 2026\, the ceremony offers a meaningful opportunity to recognize the 
 individuals and events that shaped the nation’s founding.\n\nBy connecti
 ng New Bern’s Revolutionary history with the constitutional protections 
 established through the Bill of Rights\, the event highlights the continui
 ng importance of understanding\, preserving\, and sharing America’s hist
 ory.\n\nThe New Bern Chapter\, Sons of the American Revolution and the Ric
 hard Dobbs Spaight Chapter NSDAR invite the community to join them for thi
 s historic occasion.\n\nGary Gillette\, President of the New Bern Chapter\
 , Sons of the American Revolution said\n\n“I welcome and encourage every
 one to join us for the historic occasion. It’s an opportunity for everyo
 ne to not only to help celebrate the events that occurred\, but to also le
 arn a bit more about our nation’s history\, and how our small town of Ne
 w Bern played such a key role in its history.”\n\nTammy Gillette\, Regen
 t of the Richard Dobbs Spaight NSDAR Chapter said “that the commemoratio
 n of the Bill of Rights and the dedication of the New Bern Resolves Plaque
  reminds us that the liberties we cherish today were secured through the c
 ourage and sacrifice of those who came before us. As we gather to honor th
 ese historic milestones\, we celebrate not only our nation's founding prin
 ciples but also New Bern's unique place in the story of our American freed
 om. It is our responsibility to preserve this legacy and inspire future ge
 nerations to uphold the rights and responsibilities of what our forefather
 s fought for."\n\nEvent Information\n\nEvent: U.S. Bill of Rights Day Comm
 emoration and New Bern Resolves Granite & Bronze Marker Dedication\n\nDate
 : Tuesday\, December 15\, 2026\n\nTime: 2:00 p.m.\n\nLocation: Patriot Squ
 are at City Hall\, 300 Pollock Street\, New Bern\, North Carolina\n\nPrese
 nted by: New Bern Chapter\, Sons of the American Revolution and the Richar
 d Dobbs Spaight Chapter NSDAR\n\nProgram Highlights: Bill of Rights histor
 ical presentation\, dedication of the New Bern Resolves Granite & Bronze M
 arker\, and ceremonial musket volleys by the New Bern Chapter SAR Musket C
 adre.  Refreshments served afterwards.
GEO:35.106879;-77.038485
LOCATION:Patriot Square at City Hall\, Outside
SUMMARY: Bill of Rights Day Commemoration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/new-bern-to-celebrate-bill-o
 f-rights-day-with-historic-new-bern-resolves-marker-dedication
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
