BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"NC Botanical Garden": "https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/nature-tales-story-time/2027-03-19/2/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncbg": "https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/nature-tales-story-time/2027-03-19/1/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncbg
X-SOURCE:NC Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270319T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270319T110000
DTSTAMP:20261120T162309Z
CREATED:20261120T162309Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261120T162309Z
UID:10000892-1805450400-1805454000@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Nature Tales Story Time
DESCRIPTION:Bring your little one for a morning or afternoon of stories\, songs\, and outdoor discovery! Nature Tales is a monthly family program for children ages 3-7 and a grown-up\, where a nature-themed story comes to life through hands-on exploration in the garden.\n Who? Children ages 3-7\, with an adult When? 10 a.m. to 11 a.m. or 3:30 p.m. to 4:30 p.m. Where? North Carolina Botanical Garden Cost? $5 per child (free for members and families receiving SNAP benefits) \nKnow a family who’d love this? Share the event!  \nUpcoming Dates: \nFriday\, December 11th – Where Did Everyone Go? \nWhere do animals go when winter arrives? Some migrate\, some hibernate\, some stay busy all winter\, and some find cozy places to hide. After the story\, head outside to look for clues that animals are still around\, even when we don’t see them! The program will happen rain or shine\, with indoor activities if the weather is unfavorable. Register here for morning session or afternoon session. \nMore dates to come! Check back soon.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/nature-tales-story-time/2027-03-19/1/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/11/IMG_5861-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=North Carolina Botanical Garden 100 Old Mason Farm Road Chapel Hill NC 27517 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=100 Old Mason Farm Road:geo:-79.031939,35.901081
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/foundations-of-applied-mixed-methods-research-design"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261121T064456Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54364870114852
DTSTART:20270319T140000Z
DTEND:20270319T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:This workshop provides participants with practical instruction 
 on the topics of integrating qualitative and quantitative data\, and the e
 ssential principles behind designing fundable mixed methods research. Spec
 ific topics include crafting mixed methods objectives and research questio
 ns\, choosing appropriate sampling strategies\, and selecting the most eff
 ective data collection methods (qualitative and quantitative). A significa
 nt amount of time is spent demonstrating the nuts and bolts of integrating
  qualitative and quantitative datasets\, including diagramming points of i
 nterface. Although this workshop is primarily embedded in an applied conte
 xt\, the instructors will present some of the more common typologies and n
 omenclature used in the field. Course structure includes lecture\, interac
 tive discussion\, and hands-on exercises.\n\nRegistration and fee (refunda
 ble for UNCCH students upon attendance) are required for Zoom access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Foundations of Applied Mixed Methods Research Design
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/foundations-of-applied-mixed-m
 ethods-research-design
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
